262	  /* R6 §3, two stacked causes, both fixed here:
263	     1) .showcase-side's natural content (all 5/6 rows, R5's rise-mask kept
264	        every body visible at once) was taller than the embed cell's
265	        explicit height. A CSS grid item with an explicit height does not
266	        stretch to match a taller sibling's row track - the TRACK grows to
267	        fit the tall side instead, leaving the embed cell short of the
268	        row's actual height by the difference (measured ~110px), exposing
269	        the stage's own black gap background below the frame. Pinning both
270	        columns to the SAME explicit height (with the side's own
271	        overflow-y:auto as a never-clip safety net) makes them structurally
272	        impossible to mismatch, regardless of how much text a future edit
273	        adds.
274	     2) That explicit height was `100svh - 48px`, sized to sit BELOW the
275	        48px sticky topline - but the pin (`start:'top top'`) puts the
276	        section's rendered top at the viewport's own y:0, with the topline
277	        merely painted on top of (not offsetting) its first 48px. The
278	        result: content correctly avoids the topline visually, but then
279	        runs 48px short of the viewport's bottom edge, showing the stage's
280	        black background as a trailing band under both columns (measured:
281	        embed/side bottom at 852 of a 900-tall viewport). Hero's own pin
282	        has this identical 48px arithmetic and gap - invisible there only
283	        because it lands on the page's own black background either side.
284	        Showcase's is visible because there's real content flush above it.
285	        Fixed the same way hero's is invisible: fill the FULL viewport
286	        (100svh) - the topline still visually covers the top 48px (it's
287	        position:sticky, z-index:40, opaque), but the bottom now lands
288	        exactly on the viewport edge, so no gap is left to expose. */
