298	/* R6 §1/§2: replaced the "every row's full body always in the DOM,
299	   rise-mask reveal" layout (which had no height limit and let row 2's
300	   body run past its cell's bottom - real, measured clipping, not a near
301	   miss) with a scroll-driven ledger: every row always shows its heading;
302	   only the ACTIVE row expands its body via a height reveal. Collapsed rows
303	   can never overflow because they have no body box to overflow - this is
304	   what actually guarantees "no text may ever be clipped", not a taller
305	   cell. Desktop/tablet only (see the max-width:767px override below) -
306	   mobile keeps every body visible, per spec. */
307	/* flex:1 (not just auto height) so the five/six rows always share the
308	   FULL height of the ledger column between them - without it the rows'
309	   own natural (mostly collapsed) height left empty space at the bottom of
310	   the column, showing the flex container's own black gap background
311	   (a smaller instance of the same "dead band" defect as R6 §6). */
312	/* R6 bugfix: `min-height:0` let flex:1 SHRINK a row below its own content
313	   (needed to grow rows into leftover space, but it also let the browser
314	   squeeze a merely-taller-by-a-few-px collapsed heading below its natural
315	   line height when six rows shared a shorter 800px column - measured
316	   2-19px of real overflow on Hoerai's rows at 1280x800). Leaving min-height
317	   at its flex default (auto = content size) means a row can grow but never
318	   shrink below what its own heading needs; any genuine total shortfall
319	   falls through to .showcase-side's own overflow-y:auto (a scrollbar,
320	   never silent clipping). */
